# Python bytecode from tools/artwork/. The cleaner itself is committed (it is how authored and
# contributed art is converted to the TGA the client loads); its compiled cache is not.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Machine-local state from tools/artwork/artwork_cleaner.py:
#
#   .stamps  what each output was last built from, so an edited erase box or a changed --size
#            reconverts instead of being skipped as up to date. Rebuildable, and meaningless on
#            another machine.
#   .root    written by the retired manifest importer, which the cleaner replaced; nothing writes it
#            now, and it stays ignored so a stale copy on an old checkout cannot be committed.
#
# .tmp is the atomic-write staging file; it exists only mid-write.
tools/artwork/manifest.tsv.root
tools/artwork/.stamps.tsv
tools/artwork/*.tmp

# The poster's staging file. Every tool here writes .tmp then os.replace()s, but make_poster.py is
# the one that stages OUTSIDE tools/, next to its output, so the glob above cannot cover it. Only an
# interrupted run leaves it behind.
media/poster/*.tmp
